 "answer": "**I’d have her skip the outdoor walk this morning, Saturday, October 17.** Singapore’s NEA forecasts the 24-hour PSI at **150–230 (Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy)** and advises older adults to **minimise outdoor activity**. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nShe could walk indoors instead. If she’s considering going out anyway, check the **latest 1-hour PM2.5** for her area in NEA’s myENV app first; NEA advises older adults to avoid all outdoor activity for the next hour when PM2.5 is in the High band. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nIt’s also expected to get hot later, with a high around **34°C**, so avoid strenuous outdoor exercise. ([weather.gov.sg](https://www.weather.gov.sg/home))",
